.\" Generated by tools/gen_man.py from packagingonlinux/cli.py: do not edit.
.TH PACKAGINGONLINUX 1 "" "PackagingOnLinux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
packagingonlinux \- package a prebuilt application as deb, rpm, tarball, appimage, flatpak, snap, zip, nsis
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpackagingonlinux\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
\fBpackagingonlinux\fR \fB\-\-help\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Package a prebuilt application (a binary or an install folder, one per platform) into Linux and Windows formats, without root and from any distribution. The app is described once in a packaging.toml file (see packaging.toml(5)), shared by this command, the graphical interface and CI.
.PP
Every command also accepts \fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS init
\fBpackagingonlinux init\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.PP
Ask for the executable, name, id, version, maintainer, license, icon, category and formats, then write a [linux] config. Refuses to overwrite an existing file.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
path to the config (default: packaging.toml in the current directory); for check and build, \- reads it from standard input, with paths relative to the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
overwrite the config if it exists
.SS doctor
\fBpackagingonlinux doctor\fR
.PP
Print the version, then one line per format: ok, or the missing tools and the command that installs them, and a last line telling whether Docker can be used for \-\-container. Always exits 0.
.SS check
\fBpackagingonlinux check\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR]
.PP
Report missing or invalid fields and files, then generate the Linux .desktop and AppStream metainfo files in a temporary directory and run desktop\-file\-validate and appstreamcli on them (skipped when not installed). Builds and writes nothing.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
path to the config (default: packaging.toml in the current directory); for check and build, \- reads it from standard input, with paths relative to the current directory
.SS build
\fBpackagingonlinux build\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-f\fR \fIFORMATS\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-container\fR]
.PP
For each platform that has a requested format, run its build command, then build every requested format into the output directory. A format that fails, or whose tools are missing, does not stop the others: failures are listed at the end and the exit status is 1. With \-\-container, the default on Windows, the Linux build command and formats run in a Docker container (all of them but snap), so they can be built from Windows or from a machine without their tools; the Windows ones still run on the host. The container sees only the config's folder and the output directory.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
path to the config (default: packaging.toml in the current directory); for check and build, \- reads it from standard input, with paths relative to the current directory
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fIFORMATS\fR
comma\-separated formats to build (default: [output] formats of the config)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIDIR\fR
output directory (default: [output] dir of the config)
.TP
\fB\-\-container\fR, \fB\-\-no\-container\fR
build the Linux formats in a Docker container, or never (default: in a container on Windows only). Fails if Docker is missing or not running
.SS gui
\fBpackagingonlinux gui\fR [\fICONFIG\fR]
.PP
Open the graphical interface (in French), on CONFIG if given. Needs PyQt6 or PySide6.
.TP
\fICONFIG\fR
packaging.toml to open
.SH FORMATS
Values accepted by \fB\-f\fR and by [output] formats.
.TP
\fBdeb\fR
Debian / Ubuntu (.deb), from [linux]; needs dpkg\-deb.
.br
Install: apt install dpkg  (or build with \-\-container)
.TP
\fBrpm\fR
Fedora / openSUSE / RHEL (.rpm), from [linux]; needs rpmbuild.
.br
Install: dnf install rpm\-build  |  apt install rpm  (or build with \-\-container)
.TP
\fBtarball\fR
tar.gz, from [linux].
.TP
\fBappimage\fR
AppImage (.AppImage), from [linux]; needs mksquashfs.
.br
Install: apt install squashfs\-tools  |  dnf install squashfs\-tools
.TP
\fBflatpak\fR
Flatpak (.flatpak), from [linux]; needs flatpak, flatpak\-builder.
.br
Install: apt install flatpak flatpak\-builder librsvg2\-common  |  dnf install flatpak\-builder
.TP
\fBsnap\fR
Snap (.snap), from [linux]; needs snapcraft.
.br
Install: snap install snapcraft \-\-classic
.TP
\fBzip\fR
Windows portable (.zip), from [windows].
.TP
\fBnsis\fR
Windows installer (setup.exe), from [windows]; needs makensis.
.br
Install: apt install nsis  |  dnf install mingw32\-nsis  |  pacman \-S nsis (AUR)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
check found a problem, a format failed to build, init refused to overwrite a file, or the GUI is not available
.TP
\fB2\fR
invalid command line or config (unreadable packaging.toml, unknown format...), or Docker missing or not running for \-\-container
.TP
\fB130\fR
interrupted (Ctrl+C)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBPACKAGINGONLINUX_APPIMAGE_RUNTIME\fR
path to an AppImage type2 runtime to use instead of downloading the pinned release
.TP
\fBXDG_CACHE_HOME\fR
where the downloaded AppImage runtime is cached (default: ~/.cache)
.TP
\fBPACKAGINGONLINUX_CONTAINER_IMAGE\fR
image to run with \-\-container instead of building PackagingOnLinux's own (e.g. one derived from it, with the compiler that [linux] command needs)
.SH FILES
.TP
packaging.toml
the config read by default, in the current directory
.TP
$XDG_CACHE_HOME/packagingonlinux/
cache of the AppImage runtime
.TP
packagingonlinux\-cache (Docker volume)
with \-\-container: cache of the AppImage runtime and of the Flatpak runtimes
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux init\fR
Write a packaging.toml in the current directory, asking questions.
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux doctor\fR
List the formats this machine can build, and how to get the others.
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux check \-c app/packaging.toml\fR
Validate a config without building anything.
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux build\fR
Build the formats listed in [output] formats of ./packaging.toml.
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux build \-f deb,rpm \-o dist\fR
Build only the deb and rpm packages, into dist/.
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux build \-\-container\fR
Build the Linux formats in a Docker container (the default on Windows).
.TP
\fBpackagingonlinux gui app/packaging.toml\fR
Edit a config in the graphical interface.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR packaging.toml (5)
